L0266: Write or dereference lacks permission

The place is not writable through this reference, or the dereference is not supported for the receiver type. A shared reference cannot be used to assign its referent. Obtain a mutable loan of the proper owner or change the operation to an observation.

Example from `tests/corpus/reject/star_self_misused.lc`; the full file is a regression test.

```locus
// `*self` is the value behind a reference receiver: written whole through
// `&mut self`, read through either. Anything else is refused with rustc's
// code where rustc has one.
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]
struct Counter {
    count: u8,
}

impl Counter {
    fn set(&self, v: u8) -> () {
        *self = Counter { count: v };
    }

    fn set_field(&self, v: u8) -> () {
        self.count = v;
    }

    fn by_value(self) -> u8 {
        (*self).count
    }

    fn field(&self) -> u8 {
        *self.count
    }
}
```

Language, as built: [1.26:2](../../atlas.html#/doc/language/spec-1.26:2).
